  "sourceTextExcerpts": [
    {
      "ref": "1SA 1:20",
      "text": "When the time had come, Hannah conceived, and bore a son; and she named him Samuel, saying, “Because I have asked him of the LORD.”",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA01.htm#V20"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 2:18",
      "text": "But Samuel ministered before the LORD, being a child, clothed with a linen ephod.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA02.htm#V18"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 2:21",
      "text": "The LORD visited Hannah, and she conceived and bore three sons and two daughters. The child Samuel grew before the LORD.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA02.htm#V21"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 2:26",
      "text": "The child Samuel grew on, and increased in favor both with the LORD and also with men.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA02.htm#V26"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 3:1",
      "text": "The child Samuel ministered to the LORD before Eli. The LORD’s word was rare in those days. There were not many visions, then.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA03.htm#V1"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 3:20",
      "text": "All Israel from Dan even to Beersheba knew that Samuel was established to be a prophet of the LORD.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA03.htm#V20"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 7:15",
      "text": "Samuel judged Israel all the days of his life.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA07.htm#V15"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 10:1",
      "text": "Then Samuel took the vial of oil and poured it on his head, then kissed him and said, “Hasn’t the LORD anointed you to be prince over his inheritance?",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA10.htm#V1"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1SA 25:1",
      "text": "Samuel died; and all Israel gathered themselves together and mourned for him, and buried him at his house at Ramah. Then David arose and went down to the wilderness of Paran.",
      "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1SA25.htm#V1"
    }
  ],
